# Playlist Syncer

# General

- **Package manager**: bun (use `bun add`, `bun run`, etc.)
- **Stack**: TanStack Start, React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS
- **Lint/format**: Biome (bun check:fix)
- **Imports**: use `#/` alias for `./src/*`
- copy always in english

# Code Rules

- Always use the design system colors. Only use hardcoded color values if it really makes sense
- Never modify shadcn components in src/components/ui (use className prop instead)
- Never create React components inside other components
- Never use barrel exports
- Never remove comments
- Never change copy language unless explicitly asked to
- Prefer types over interfaces
- Use @/ for src imports
- Extract inline conditionals to explanatory variables (e.g., `const hasData = data && data.length > 0`)
- Break large components into smaller, cohesive sub-components:
  - Keep sub-components in the same file if not reusable elsewhere
  - Create separate files only for reusable components

# Naming Conventions

- Files: kebab-case (research-assistant.tsx)
- Components: PascalCase (ResearchAssistant)
- Functions/variables: camelCase (generateScript)
- Constants: UPPER_CASE (API_KEY)
- Types: PascalCase (ScriptResponse)

# Architecture

Backend structure (src/server/api/):

- Routers: Controllers that call use cases
- Use cases: Business logic, DB operations, External API calls
- Services: Shared utilities

# Design Principles

- Clean, simple, consistent
- Leverage Shadcn components
- Don't reinvent the wheel

# 🚨 DATABASE RULES

- NEVER use `drizzle-kit push`
- NEVER use schema sync commands
- ALWAYS use migrations
- If schema changes are needed, create a new migration only